284: ## Cross-subject
285: 
286: No music 9 to 12 row carries a cross_subject lean (data/progressions/arts.csv), so this course waits on no other
287: course and no other course waits on it. STANDARD.md 6's music and math lean (note values on fractions) is met by
288: grade 5. The contacts below are practiced, not owned, each with its "if later" line; all are core courses (lesson
289: 32). A Level is open to any grade, so no contact assumes a unit of a given grade's core course.
290: 
291: ### English language arts, grades 9 to 12
292: 
293: | Used here | Contact | If English language arts has not taught it yet |
294: |---|---|---|
295: | Units 4, 9 and 14 (interpretations), units 5, 10 and 15 (critiques), unit 17 (reviews) | Argument writing with claims and evidence (W.9-10.1, W.11-12.1): practiced, not owned | Each unit's step card gives the claim, evidence from the music, reasoning frame and a worked example; the music guide marks the musical evidence, not the writing standard |
296: 
297: ### Mathematics
298: 
299: No unit asks for number work past grade 5 (lesson 13): durations are counted in beats and fractions of a beat;
300: frequency ratios and the overtone series are out.
301: 
302: ### Social studies and science
303: 
304: Works are taught with their time and place on our own work cards (bar criterion 7), with no lean on a social
305: studies unit. A capstone (unit 18) that ties music to a science of sound or a history uses only what the student
306: has already studied in that course, chosen with the teacher.
