## Seams

### Picked up from Music, grades 6 to 8

Each Level 1 row assumes its grade 8 row (data/progressions/arts.csv). Music, grades 6 to 8 is a band course whose
grade 8 year ends that course; its unit numbers are not cited here. Level 1 meets each as a readiness check (see
Readiness and retrieval) after the bridge has taught its techniques and words.

| Grade 8 row hands on | Level 1 row that picks it up (unit) | What Level 1 does with it |
|---|---|---|
| mu-g8-invent | mu-g9-invent (unit 2) | Composes from an outside idea (a mood, image or story) with no set form, where grade 8 built phrases inside a given expanded form |
| mu-g8-document | mu-g9-document (unit 3) | Traces a short idea across three or more dated drafts, where grade 8 documented one finished piece |
| mu-g8-revise | mu-g9-revise (unit 4) | Revises with the teacher's criteria and adds the setting and medium to the revision note |
| mu-g8-read | mu-g9-read (unit 3) | Analyzes model works by ear for composing, where grade 8 read and compared scores to perform them |
| mu-g8-express | mu-g9-express (unit 4) | Writes an interpretation citing genre and technique as evidence for the composer's aim |
| mu-g8-perform | mu-g9-perform (unit 5) | Writes a rehearsal plan and performs the student's own and others' works, live or recorded |
| mu-g8-choose | mu-g9-choose (unit 2) | Chooses passages as models for composing, logging how tastes and skills shaped each pick |
| mu-g8-respond | mu-g9-respond (unit 5) | Critiques with basic theory terms and says what a classmate's feedback changes in the student's own piece |

