| Level 1 year-end (week 32, days 159 and 160) | 5 | 1 | 1 | Samples units 3 and 4 in a sitting: a by-ear form analysis of an unseen public domain work with one rehearsal step (MU:Re7.2.C.Ia, MU:Pr4.2.C.Ia), a written interpretation of an unseen work's aim (MU:Re8.1.C.Ia), and a given flawed 8-bar draft improved against the teacher's criteria (MU:Cr3.1.C.Ia). Unit 5 is assessed by its own showing; its concert record is carried unscored. Respond on day 160. |
| Level 2 mid-year (week 16, days 239 and 240) | 8 | 1 | 1 | Samples unit 7: a fresh sketch from a given short text with its stated aim (MU:Cr1.1.C.IIa, MU:Cr2.1.C.IIa) and a defended pick from two unseen movements (MU:Pr4.1.C.IIa, MU:Re7.1.C.IIa). Unit 8's annotated log record is carried unscored. Respond on day 240. |
| Level 2 year-end (week 32, days 319 and 320) | 10 | 1 | 1 | Samples units 8 and 9: a score analysis of an unseen public domain excerpt with its function and a rehearsal choice (MU:Re7.2.C.IIa, MU:Pr4.2.C.IIa), a supported interpretation of an unseen work (MU:Re8.1.C.IIa), and a given draft improved against stated criteria with a short defense (MU:Cr3.1.C.IIa). Unit 10 is assessed by its own showing. Respond on day 320. |
| Level 3 mid-year (week 16, days 399 and 400) | 13 | 1 | 1 | Samples unit 12: a fresh extended sketch of a given abstract idea (MU:Cr1.1.C.IIIa, MU:Cr2.1.C.IIIa) and a justified pick of a section from an unseen whole short work (MU:Pr4.1.C.IIIa, MU:Re7.1.C.IIIa). Unit 13's annotated log record is carried unscored. Respond on day 400. |
| Level 3 year-end (week 32, days 479 and 480) | 15 | 1 | 1 | Samples units 13 and 14: a score analysis of an unseen public domain excerpt with a defended rehearsal choice (MU:Re7.2.C.IIIa, MU:Pr4.2.C.IIIa), a reading of an unseen work defended against a given other reading (MU:Re8.1.C.IIIa), and a given draft improved against criteria the student states from research done in unit 14 (MU:Cr3.1.C.IIIa). Unit 15 is assessed by its own showings. Respond on day 480. |
