{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'mu-g8-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.8a; MU:Cr3.1.8b; MU:Cr3.2.8a', 'assumes': 'mu-g7-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g9-revise', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'technique; justify; polish; tension; release; balance', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Revise a piece with criteria the student picks (technique, style, form, sound sources), justify the final polish against them, and present the notated piece. What changes: the student justifies each choice against criteria. Assessed by a presented piece and a written justification scored on a rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'mu-g8-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.8a; MU:Pr4.2.8b; MU:Pr4.2.8c', 'assumes': 'mu-g7-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g9-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'sight-read; treble staff; bass staff; compare; build; effect', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Compare how two contrasting performance pieces are built, sight-read simple rhythm, melody or harmony lines on treble or bass staves, and explain how culture and history change the way each is played. What changes: the student reads new notation at sight on treble or bass staves, where grade 7 read familiar pieces. Assessed by a sight-reading task and a written comparison, scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'mu-g8-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.8a; MU:Re8.1.8a', 'assumes': 'mu-g7-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g9-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'program; reading; back; evidence; interpretation; convey', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Perform contrasting pieces and explain how the student's interpretation carries the music's intent, and write an argument with evidence about how a whole program carries intent. What changes: readings are backed with evidence across a whole program. Assessed by a performance and a written argument with evidence, scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'mu-g8-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.8a; MU:Pr6.1.8a; MU:Pr6.1.8b', 'assumes': 'mu-g7-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g9-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'own criteria; style; culturally authentic; honor; venue; ready', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Rehearse with the student's own criteria, decide when the music is ready, and perform it accurately, in style and with practice true to its culture, with manners that fit the event and venue. What changes: the student writes the criteria and authentic practice is added. Assessed by a performance and a readiness note scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'mu-g8-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.8a; MU:Re7.1.8a; MU:Cn10.1.8a', 'assumes': 'mu-g7-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g9-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'program; own criteria; mix; select; interest; contrast', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Build and explain a program of contrasting music with the student's own criteria, such as a themed mix, and show how it ties to the student's interests. What changes: the student sets the criteria and builds a program. Assessed by a program note scored on a rubric. Every personal tie has an invented or public option beside it, marked the same (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground)."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '8', 'skill_id': 'mu-g8-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re7.2.8a; MU:Re7.2.8b; MU:Re9.1.8a; MU:Cn11.1.8a', 'assumes': 'mu-g7-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g9-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'program; compare; own criteria; setting; evidence; connect', 'cross_subject': 'ela:W.8.1 (an argument supported by evidence)', 'notes': 'Compare whole programs of music from many genres, cultures and eras, explaining how elements and expression connect to structure and naming each setting, judge them with criteria the student writes, and link the music to another art or subject. What changes: whole programs are compared and the student writes the criteria, where grade 7 compared pairs of pieces. Assessed by a written argument with evidence scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.C.Ia; MU:Cr2.1.C.Ia', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-invent', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'sketch; motif; mood; storyline; represent; aim', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Pick a mood, image or story, collect short sound ideas that could stand for it in an idea bank, and arrange the best into a first sketch with a one-line aim. What changes: the student composes from an outside idea with no set form, where grade 8 built phrases inside a given expanded form. Assessed by a sketch with a one-line aim, scored on a short rubric for the idea, its link to the aim and range. Level 1 bridge: the first unit teaches the grade 8 techniques and words Level 1 needs, as readiness, and claims no grade 8 id (at most 12 days in the full year, 6 on the 80-day short path, STANDARD.md 3.2).'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.C.Ib', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-document', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'draft; binary; cyclical; one-part; develop; motif', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Develop a short idea through three or more dated drafts in a simple form (one-part, cyclical or binary) and describe in the draft log how it grew. What changes: the student traces growth across drafts, where grade 8 documented one finished piece. Assessed by a draft log scored on a short rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.C.Ia; MU:Cr3.2.C.Ia; MU:Cr3.2.C.Ib', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-revise', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'criteria; final version; medium; context; share; intent', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Revise drafts to a final version with the teacher's criteria, share it as a score, a performance or a recording, and write a short note on how its elements serve the aim and how the given setting and medium shape it. What changes: the setting and medium join the revision. Assessed by a final version, its draft trail and a short note on setting, scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.C.Ia; MU:Re7.2.C.Ia', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'analyze; form; style; mood; aural; model', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Listen to model works and mark, by ear, how their elements and form fit the style and mood, then write what that means for rehearsing them and for the student's own composing. What changes: analysis serves composing, where grade 8 read and compared scores to perform them. Assessed by a listening analysis scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.C.Ia; MU:Re8.1.C.Ia', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'interpret; genre; intent; technical; expressive; evidence', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write an interpretation of a work from its elements, style and mood, naming the composer's aim and backing it with technical and expressive evidence and the genre. What changes: genre and technique are cited as evidence for the aim. Assessed by a short written interpretation scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.C.Ia; MU:Pr5.1.C.Ib; MU:Pr5.1.C.Ic; MU:Pr6.1.C.Ia; MU:Pr6.1.C.Ib', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'rehearsal plan; repetition; variation; recorded; audience; feedback', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write a rehearsal plan that marks repetition and variation in a piece, rehearse own and others' works with set criteria and feedback, and share a live or recorded performance with a note on how it suits its audience or setting. What changes: the works performed include the student's own compositions, live or recorded, so no instrument is needed. Assessed by a rehearsal plan and a take with a short note, scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it. Teacher note: no student is recorded, photographed or filmed without the family's yes; a face or voice is never required (hands, the work or the sound alone will do); a student who does not want to be recorded is observed live and the teacher's mark stands; kept work stays on the student's, family's or school's own device."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.C.Ia; MU:Re7.1.C.Ia; MU:Cn10.0.C.Ia', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'excerpt; passage; model; select; criteria; interest', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Use the teacher's criteria to choose passages and short pieces in simple forms that carry a mood, image or story as models for composing, logging each pick and how the student's tastes and skills shaped it. What changes: pieces are chosen as models for the student's own composing. Assessed by a model-piece log with reasons, scored on a short rubric. Model pieces come from more than one culture and era, living composers among them. Every personal tie has an invented or public option beside it, marked the same (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground)."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '9', 'skill_id': 'mu-g9-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re9.1.C.Ia; MU:Re9.1.C.Ib; MU:Cn11.0.C.Ia', 'assumes': 'mu-g8-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g10-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'effectiveness; theory; critique; feedback; fundamentals; relate', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Critique pieces and performances with basic theory terms, give and take feedback on a classmate's composition and note what it changes in the student's own, and link a piece to another art, subject or setting. What changes: judgment uses music theory terms. Assessed by a written critique with evidence, scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.C.IIa; MU:Cr2.1.C.IIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-invent', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'sonic event; memory; concept; text; sketch; expressive', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Start from a memory, a text, a concept or a sound event, collect sound ideas that stand for it, and arrange many of them into a first expressive sketch with a stated aim. What changes: sources widen to memories, concepts and texts, where level 1 used a mood, image or story. Assessed by a sketch with a stated aim, scored on the Level 2 rubric. Level 2 opens with a review unit of at most 6 days that serves as placement.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.C.IIb', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-document', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'rondo; ternary; binary; draft; develop; explain', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Develop an idea through dated drafts in a binary, rondo or ternary form and explain in an annotated log how and why it grew. What changes: rondo and ternary join, and the student explains the growth, where level 1 described it. Assessed by an annotated draft log scored on the Level 2 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.C.IIa; MU:Cr3.2.C.IIa; MU:Cr3.2.C.IIb', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-revise', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'own criteria; compositional technique; medium; context; final version; justify', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Revise drafts to a final version with given or self-chosen criteria, share it by score, solo or group performance or technology, and defend in a short note how its elements and composing techniques serve the aim and why the chosen setting and medium suit it. What changes: the student picks the criteria, the setting and the medium. Assessed by a final version and a short defence, scored on the Level 2 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.C.IIa; MU:Re7.2.C.IIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'score; function; context; procedure; technique; analyze', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Study model works by ear and from the score, marking elements, form and composing techniques against style, function and setting, and write what they model for rehearsal and for the student's own writing. What changes: scores, function and composing techniques join the analysis. Assessed by a score and listening analysis scored on the Level 2 rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.C.IIa; MU:Re8.1.C.IIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'function; context; support; genre; intent; interpretation', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write an interpretation of a work that ties its elements, form, techniques, genre and setting to the composer's aim, with support from the music. What changes: function and setting now support the reading. Assessed by a written interpretation scored on the Level 2 rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.C.IIa; MU:Pr5.1.C.IIb; MU:Pr5.1.C.IIc; MU:Pr6.1.C.IIa; MU:Pr6.1.C.IIb', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'formal design; historical context; style; rehearsal plan; audience; varied', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write rehearsal plans that name form, style and the work's historical or cultural setting, rehearse varied works with criteria and feedback, and share a performance with a note on how its techniques carry the aim and suit both audience and setting. What changes: style and setting enter the rehearsal plan. Assessed by a rehearsal plan and a take with a note, scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it. Teacher note: no student is recorded, photographed or filmed without the family's yes; a face or voice is never required (hands, the work or the sound alone will do); a student who does not want to be recorded is observed live and the teacher's mark stands; kept work stays on the student's, family's or school's own device."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.C.IIa; MU:Re7.1.C.IIa; MU:Cn10.0.C.IIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'movement; defend; model; criteria; moderately complex; interest', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Choose passages or movements in simple or moderately complex forms as models for composing, with given or self-set criteria, and defend each pick in a log that also says how the student's tastes and skills shaped it. What changes: the student may set the criteria and defends each choice. Assessed by a model-piece log with a defence, scored on the Level 2 rubric. Model pieces come from more than one culture and era, living composers among them. Every personal tie has an invented or public option beside it, marked the same (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground)."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '10', 'skill_id': 'mu-g10-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re9.1.C.IIa; MU:Re9.1.C.IIb; MU:Cn11.0.C.IIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g9-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g11-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'theory; procedure; critique; feedback; applied; relate', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Critique pieces and performances with theory and composing-technique terms, show in the student's own drafts where critique given and feedback received changed the work, and link a piece to another art, subject or setting. What changes: the student points to where feedback changed their own work. Assessed by a written critique scored on the Level 2 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.C.IIIa; MU:Cr2.1.C.IIIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-studio', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'abstract; extended; sonic experience; sketch; multiple; represent', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Choose an abstract idea or an extended experience, sketch several ways sound could stand for it, and arrange extended ideas into a first expressive sketch with a stated aim. What changes: the subject is abstract or extended and chosen by the student, where level 2 worked from events, texts and concepts. Assessed by a sketch with a stated aim, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Level 3 opens with a review unit of at most 6 days that serves as placement.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.C.IIIb', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-studio', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'complex form; extended; analyze; draft; develop; demonstrate', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Develop extended ideas through dated drafts in moderately complex and complex forms, and analyze in an annotated log how the material grew. What changes: complex forms, and analysis where level 2 explained. Assessed by an annotated draft log scored on the Level 3 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.C.IIIa; MU:Cr3.2.C.IIIa; MU:Cr3.2.C.IIIb', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-studio', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'research; process; compare; medium; context; final version', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Research criteria and use them to revise drafts to a final version, share it with a note on how its elements, techniques and process serve the aim, and compare two or three possible settings and mediums before choosing one. What changes: criteria come from research, and settings are compared before one is chosen. Assessed by a final version and a comparison note, scored on the Level 3 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.C.IIIa; MU:Re7.2.C.IIIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-criticism', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'aesthetic effectiveness; procedure; score; defend; analysis; context', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Analyze model works by ear and from the score, weighing their techniques and procedures against style, mood, setting and effect, and defend the analysis and the rehearsal choices it leads to. What changes: the effect of the music is weighed and the analysis is defended. Assessed by a score and listening analysis scored on the Level 3 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.C.IIIa; MU:Re8.1.C.IIIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-perform; mu-g12-criticism', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'justify; defend; interpretation; genre; context; intent', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Write and defend an interpretation of varied works from their form, techniques, genre and setting, set against another reading of the same work. What changes: the student defends a reading against another one. Assessed by a written interpretation scored on the Level 3 rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.C.IIIa; MU:Pr5.1.C.IIIb; MU:Pr5.1.C.IIIc; MU:Pr6.1.C.IIIa; MU:Pr6.1.C.IIIb', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'contrasting; compositional technique; variety of audiences; compare; strategy; convey', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Write rehearsal plans naming form, variation, composing techniques, style and setting, rehearse contrasting works with criteria and feedback and compare practice methods, and share performances with a note on how the aim comes across to different audiences and settings. What changes: contrasting works and many audiences. Assessed by a rehearsal plan and a take with a note, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it. Teacher note: no student is recorded, photographed or filmed without the family's yes; a face or voice is never required (hands, the work or the sound alone will do); a student who does not want to be recorded is observed live and the teacher's mark stands; kept work stays on the student's, family's or school's own device."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '11', 'skill_id': 'mu-g11-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.C.IIIa; MU:Re7.1.C.IIIa; MU:Cn10.0.C.IIIa', 'assumes': 'mu-g10-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g12-connect', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'researched criteria; entire work; complex form; justify; model; interest', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Choose sections, movements or whole works in complex forms as models for composing, with researched or self-set criteria, and justify each pick in a log that also says how the student's tastes and skills shaped it. What changes: whole works and researched criteria. Assessed by a model-piece log with reasons, scored on the Level 3 rubric. Model pieces come from more than one culture and era, living composers among them. Every personal tie has an invented or public option beside it, marked the same (APPROACH.md, Sensitive ground)."}
