e check day, day 189), id by id: MU:Cr3.1.8a, a kept justification note: the draft judged on the student's own criteria; MU:Cr3.1.8b, the same note: each final choice justified against them; MU:Cr3.2.8a, a guide look-for: the final score presented with its techniques named on the program; MU:Pr5.1.8a, a kept readiness card made on the last rehearsal day: the student's criteria and the decision with a reason; MU:Pr6.1.8a, a guide look-for: "Sambalelê" or the piece performed accurately, in style and with the practice its source gives; MU:Pr6.1.8b, a guide look-for on stage and audience manners, and a short spoken item after the group's turn: one way manners in the samba de roda circle differ from the school concert. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: a rehearsal plan and recorded performance of the student's own work (Level 1). Tools: the justification note, the readiness card, the concert plan card, Curio Class's own. Free path: as unit 4. Once-a-week path: 6 sessions | Last in the band because the concert presents unit 11's piece and unit 9's pieces and ends the year; its concert is its own end-of-unit assessment (day 189, week 31); the year-end check in week 32 samples units 9 to 11; the performing and revising threads then go to Level 1 | Candidate: "true to its culture" checked against the national standard's own wording for MU:Pr6.1.8a before the unit plan's look-fors are written | Samba de roda: the agent reads UNESCO's page and a Brazilian cultural body's or educator's published teaching first; the students learn the song's practice from that source only, never by costume, accent or invented imitation, and no student dances samba as a test (dance is a different course). Performing: as unit 4. Hazards and controls: as unit 4; clapping patterns at a set level. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |

