### Handed on to Music, grades 9 to 12 (Level 1)

Level 1 is entered by any student new to music in high school, whatever their grade (STANDARD.md 3.2), so its rows
assume grade 8 and its first unit is a bridge (at most 12 days) that teaches the grade 8 techniques and words it
needs, as readiness, claiming no grade 8 id (mu-g9-invent's note). A student who finished year 8 here meets that
bridge as review. Level 1's units are those of docs/courses/music-grades-9-to-12/frame.md: its unit 1 is that
bridge (12 days, claiming no id), and its "Picked up from Music, grades 6 to 8" table names the same eight rows.

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up (Level 1 unit) | What Level 1 does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| mu-g8-invent | 11 | mu-g9-invent (unit 2) | Composes from an outside idea (a mood, image or story) with no set form, from an idea bank to a first sketch |
| mu-g8-document | 11 | mu-g9-document (unit 3) | Traces growth across three or more dated drafts in a simple form |
| mu-g8-revise | 12 | mu-g9-revise (unit 4) | Revises to a final version with the setting and medium added to the criteria |
| mu-g8-read | 9 | mu-g9-read (unit 3) | Analyzes model works by ear to serve the student's own composing |
| mu-g8-express | 10 | mu-g9-express (unit 4) | A written interpretation citing genre and technique as evidence for the composer's aim |
| mu-g8-perform | 12 | mu-g9-perform (unit 5) | A rehearsal plan, and the student's own compositions performed live or recorded |
| mu-g8-choose | 10 | mu-g9-choose (unit 2) | Passages chosen as models for the student's own composing |
| mu-g8-respond | 9 | mu-g9-respond (unit 5) | Critique with basic theory terms and feedback on a classmate's composition |

Each hand-on above is answered at both ends in data/progressions/arts.csv (the Level 1 rows' `assumes` cells).



