  written." In section 1 replace the last two sentences of the script bullet with: "It does not check that an id exists in
  the file. A plan's ids are checked by the standards gate against the file's lines (a worker's job, owed); until it
  exists, each scope and sequence states its id count against the table in section 3 and a reader spot-checks ten."
  Confidence on the gate itself is a judgment call; the stale note is firm.
# Arts pre-work: second-model cold read, 2026-11-20

> Filed by the lead 2026-11-20. Gemini 4 Neon (medium effort) in Antigravity, pasted by Cory from S:/CurioClass-gemini/ (prompt 10 to 18 for this subject), after it passed calibration (docs/reviews/calibration-*-gemini-2026-11-20.md). Its saved report is S:/CurioClass-gemini/reports/prework-arts-read.md; text unchanged here except wording the repository checks flag.

Read as the curriculum expert (docs/agents/EXPERT.md) with the arts lens (docs/agents/lenses/arts.md) against the stage 1 pre-work brief (docs/pipeline/briefs/prework-codex-read.md). I did not write these drafts. Nothing in the repository was edited; this report is saved to S:\CurioClass-gemini\reports\prework-arts-read.md. Outside sources were checked by web search and are linked below; anything resting on memory is marked "from memory". Confidence is Firm, Likely or Judgment call on each finding.

## What I read

AGENTS.md; docs/agents/EXPERT.md; docs/agents/lenses/arts.md; docs/FOUNDATION.md; docs/PRODUCTION-PATH.md; docs/COURSE-RUN.md; docs/GLOSSARY.md; docs/courses/CALENDAR.md; docs/courses/UNIT-PLAN.md; docs/ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS.md (pass rule, C1 to C16, part 2 Arts, the arts row of "Before a scope and sequence", sources table); docs/courses/arts/STANDARD.md; docs/courses/arts/APPROACH.md; docs/reviews/arts-open-material-2026-11-16.md; docs/reviews/arts-hs-music-and-levels-2026-11-16.md; docs/pipeline/briefs/sensitivity-read.md; data/standards/ncas-performance-standards.txt (in full, 1,221 lines); data/standards/ncas-performance-standards-words.txt (in full, 1,123 lines); data/standards/shape-pe-2024.txt (lines 1 to 30); docs/courses/health/APPROACH.md and docs/courses/sel/APPROACH.md (finished examples); docs/reviews/prework-sel-read-2026-11-19.md (report shape); data/courses.csv (lines 28 to 32 for arts, plus SEL/ELD rows for comparison); scripts/progression.py (lines 40 to 130: STD_FILES, ANCHOR, ANCHOR_SKIP, LEVEL, code_grades); scripts/standards.py (lines 1 to 142). Opened only after all findings below were written: docs/reviews/prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md.

## Verdict

The arts pre-work is much stronger after the 2026-11-19 fixes: the 1,114 own-words lines are cleanly paraphrased, the K to 8 band-year rule and high school composition-and-theory music choice are sound, and the five day kinds and ordinary-room rules fit Curio Class. The biggest risk is that stage 2 and stage 4 writers will hit hard contradictions between the prose and the gates: a likely phantom duplicate id (`MU:Re9.1.Kb`), an unstated `grade`-column mapping for high school levels alongside a `code_grades` rule that blocks every K to 8 and Level 1 `~` carry, missing core progression skill ids in every cross-subject lean, and an `APPROACH.md` that still omits or misplaces half of `UNIT-PLAN.md`'s unit and section fields. The one change that matters most before stage 2 and stage 3 build on these pages is reconciling `STANDARD.md` with `scripts/progression.py` (ownership, `~` carry, high school `.C` music ids, and the 12-day bridge rule) while completing the missing `UNIT-PLAN.md` field map in `APPROACH.md`.

